remove build/test/state-diff from the andesim binary; add build_all + test_all

The developer subcommands leave the product binary; building and testing move
to scripts, so the release surface is just run/list/doctor.

- main.cpp: drop build/test/state-diff and the "developer commands" section
  (and the now-unused Tier::Dev). Dispatch + help shrink to run/list/doctor.
- delete cmd_build.cpp; drop the cmd_state_diff CLI wrapper but KEEP
  diff_states()/print_diff_report() -- the compare core still backs
  run --verify and run --cosim.
- repoint the "run ./andesim build" hints in cmd_doctor.cpp,
  engine_registry.hpp, and hsim.py (doctor parity) to scripts/build_all.sh.
- tests/e2e.sh: drop the VERIFY=1 oracle block, its only andesim call, so the
  harness no longer depends on the product binary. Differential verify already
  lives in run --verify (test_andes_sim_verify.sh).

New scripts (thin wrappers; no build logic duplicated):
- scripts/build_all.sh [TARGET] [--dry-run]  == the old `build --what all`,
  delegating to setup.sh / scripts/build_*.sh / make.
- scripts/test_all.sh [--dry-run] [unit|contract|e2e]  -- C++ unit tests +
  tests/andes_sim/*.sh contracts + scripts/run_e2e.sh.

Behavioral (CLI surface) + structural (build/test relocated). TDD: the
release-surface / build_all / test_all / e2e_selfcontained contracts were
written RED first. Deleted the four tests that drove the removed
build/state-diff commands. Docs (USER_GUIDE.md, CLAUDE.md) repointed.
Unit tests 9/9, parity 2/2, contracts green.

